# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

On `/together`, when the `GET /api/duos/live` read in `CoopPanel` fails, the panel shows an alert that names the failure, plus a **Try again** button (`coop-live-retry`). This replaces today's silent `() => undefined`. Pressing Try again reads `/api/duos/live` again, and a successful read draws the `coop-rejoin` link ("Back to your co-op game"). The change copies the panel's existing saved-decks pattern (`loadError`/`retry`/`coopDecksRetry`, #1568), and all 19 existing `CoopPanel.test.tsx` tests still pass.

## Files to touch

| Path | new/change | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/duos/CoopPanel.tsx` | change | New hook `useLiveCoop()` next to `useSavedDecks`. It replaces the `live` state and the B42 mount effect, and the panel renders an alert plus Try again when the read fails. |
| `apps/web/src/duos/testids.ts` | change | New key `coopLiveRetry: "coop-live-retry"`. |
| `apps/web/src/i18n/zh-CN.json` | change | One entry for the new sentence. `i18n.test.ts` ("R711000 every sentence the client wraps in t() has a zh-CN entry") requires it. |
| `apps/web/src/duos/CoopPanel.test.tsx` | change | New `describe` with two tests. |

**Do not touch:**
- `e2e/` (its `support/testids.ts` already leaves out `coop-rejoin` and `coop-decks-retry`).
- `apps/web/src/net/duos.ts` (`getDuosLive` is already right).
- `apps/web/src/together/*`: its tests already stub `/api/duos/live` with 200, so no new alert appears there.
- `apps/web/src/duos/duos.css` (it already has `.coop-panel__error` and `.coop-panel__row`).
- Every crate, `spec/`, `crates/cards/patches/`.

**Governing rules:** this is client chrome only, so no spec section or ruling applies and no ruling is added. CLAUDE.md rule 7: the panel only shows what the server answered about the caller's own match. No patch fragment is needed, because no card plays differently (like #1910, a web-only patch).

## Steps

1. **`apps/web/src/duos/testids.ts`.** Directly after the `coopDecksRetry: "coop-decks-retry",` line (line 34), add:
   ```ts
     /** #1900: a failed read of the live co-op game offers Try again beside the alert. */
     coopLiveRetry: "coop-live-retry",
   ```

2. **`apps/web/src/duos/CoopPanel.tsx`, new hook.** Directly after the closing `}` of `useSavedDecks` (line 90) and its blank line, add this hook (an exact copy of `useSavedDecks`'s shape):
   ```ts
   /** B42: the co-op game the account is already in (null when none), and why it could not be read. */
   function useLiveCoop(): { live: string | null; liveError: string | null; retryLive: () => void } {
     const [live, setLive] = useState<string | null>(null);
     const [liveError, setLiveError] = useState<string | null>(null);
     const [attempt, setAttempt] = useState(0);
     useEffect(() => {
       let cancelled = false;
       getDuosLive().then(
         (answer) => {
           if (!cancelled) setLive(answer.matchId);
         },
         (cause: unknown) => {
           if (!cancelled) setLiveError(messageOf(cause));
         },
       );
       return () => {
         cancelled = true;
       };
     }, [attempt]);
     const retryLive = (): void => {
       setLiveError(null);
       setAttempt((before) => before + 1);
     };
     return { live, liveError, retryLive };
   }
   ```
   `getDuosLive` and `messageOf` are already imported. Add no import.

3. **`apps/web/src/duos/CoopPanel.tsx`, in `CoopPanel`.**
   1. Replace the line `const [live, setLive] = useState<string | null>(null);` (line 108) with `const { live, liveError, retryLive } = useLiveCoop();`.
   2. Delete the whole block that follows: the comment `// B42: a co-op game the account is already in is offered first.` and its `useEffect(() => { … getDuosLive() … }, []);` (lines 110–122).
   3. Leave exactly one blank line before `// The host's wait: …`.

4. **`apps/web/src/duos/CoopPanel.tsx`, JSX.** Directly after the closing `)}` of the `{live === null ? null : ( <a … coopRejoin …> )}` block (line 233), add this (a copy of the decks alert at lines 287–298):
   ```tsx
         {liveError === null ? null : (
           <>
             <p className="coop-panel__error" role="alert">
               {t("Your live co-op game could not be checked: {message}", { message: t(liveError) })}
             </p>
             <div className="coop-panel__row">
               <button type="button" data-testid={duosTestid.coopLiveRetry} onClick={retryLive}>
                 {t("Try again")}
               </button>
             </div>
           </>
         )}
   ```

5. **`apps/web/src/i18n/zh-CN.json`.** Directly after the line `"Back to your co-op game": "回到你的合作对局",` (line 1221), add:
   ```json
     "Your live co-op game could not be checked: {message}": "无法检查你正在进行的合作对局：{message}",
   ```
   - The `{message}` token must match the English key exactly; `i18n.test.ts` checks it.
   - `"Try again"` already has an entry. Add nothing for it.

6. **`apps/web/src/duos/CoopPanel.test.tsx`.** Add the block from **Tests** after the closing `});` of `describe("B60 the deck choice", …)` (line 363) and before `describe("B60 inviting a friend", …)`. It needs no new import: `serve`, `refusal`, `renderPanel`, `SLOW`, `screen` and `fireEvent` are all already in the file.

## Tests

The new block for `apps/web/src/duos/CoopPanel.test.tsx` (copy exactly):

```tsx
describe("#1900 the way back to a live co-op game", () => {
  it("#1900 a live co-op game that could not be read is named in an alert with Try again, and no way back is drawn", async () => {
    serve({ created: false, guestJoined: false }, (call) =>
      call.method === "GET" && call.path === "/api/duos/live" ? refusal(500, "internal", "The co-op games are out of reach.") : undefined,
    );
    await renderPanel();
    expect(await screen.findByRole("alert", undefined, SLOW)).toHaveTextContent(
      "Your live co-op game could not be checked: The co-op games are out of reach.",
    );
    expect(screen.getByTestId("coop-live-retry")).toHaveTextContent("Try again");
    expect(screen.queryByTestId("coop-rejoin")).toBeNull();
  });

  it("#1900 Try again reads the live co-op game again and offers the way back to it", async () => {
    let reads = 0;
    serve({ created: false, guestJoined: false }, (call) => {
      if (call.method === "GET" && call.path === "/api/duos/live") {
        reads += 1;
        return reads === 1 ? refusal(500, "internal", "The co-op games are out of reach.") : { status: 200, body: { matchId: "dm-5" } };
      }
      return undefined;
    });
    await renderPanel();
    expect(await screen.findByRole("alert", undefined, SLOW)).toHaveTextContent(
      "Your live co-op game could not be checked: The co-op games are out of reach.",
    );

    fireEvent.click(screen.getByTestId("coop-live-retry"));
    expect(await screen.findByTestId("coop-rejoin", undefined, SLOW)).toHaveAttribute("href", "/duos/dm-5");
    expect(reads).toBe(2);
    expect(screen.queryByRole("alert")).toBeNull();
    expect(screen.queryByTestId("coop-live-retry")).toBeNull();
  });
});
```

What each test proves:
- The first test proves acceptance item 1. Without the change it fails: no alert appears.
- The second test proves item 2. Without the change it fails: there is no `coop-live-retry` to click.
- In both tests the decks read succeeds, so `findByRole("alert")` finds exactly one alert.

Commands (`pnpm --dir apps/web test` builds the WebAssembly first; it needs that, and on main the build was required before vitest would run at all):
- `pnpm --dir apps/web test src/duos/CoopPanel.test.tsx`: all 21 tests pass (the 19 on main plus the 2 new ones).
- `pnpm --dir apps/web exec vitest run src/i18n/i18n.test.ts`: proves the zh-CN entry and its `{message}` token.
- `pnpm --dir apps/web typecheck`
- `pnpm exec eslint apps/web/src/duos apps/web/src/i18n`

## Done when

- [ ] A refused `GET /api/duos/live` shows a `role="alert"` naming the failure, plus a `coop-live-retry` Try again button, and no `coop-rejoin` link.

